findings.description:
Task 7.1 says an empty `base..head` range "is impossible here". It is possible when:
- the head is already merged into the base;
- head equals base, for example running on `squadron-pr` itself;
- the base is chosen as a ref the head has not advanced past.

Task 3.2 even tests that an empty range returns `[]`. In that state the "what changed" section has no commits, the Task 10a fallback ("first commit's subject, always present") has nothing to use, and `open_pull_request` gets a 422. No task refuses it before the model call. Add a refusal for an empty range. Also, `git log` is newest-first (Task 3.1), so "first commit's subject" is the newest commit. Say which one is intended.
